# Support project

Agent skill: [.cursor/skills/support-agent/SKILL.md](../skills/support-agent/SKILL.md)

## Scope

`support/frontend`, `support/backend`, `support/backend/migrations`.

## Ports and env

| Layer | Port | Env file |
|-------|------|----------|
| Frontend | 3021 | `support/frontend/.env` (`VITE_*` only) |
| Backend | 4021 | `support/backend/.env` |

Backend loads only `support/backend/.env`. Production host: `https://support.webonone.com`.

## Ownership

- Public how-tos for WebOnOne users. Help articles need no login; **`/feedback`** uses Identity JWT.
- Bug/feature reports API + `feedback_reports` table in `webonone_support`. Each report has **`ticket_number`** (four digits, `0001`…). Statuses: `todo`, `ready_to_develop`, `planned`, `in_progress`, `developed`, `staging`, `closed` (default `todo`). `/feedback-fix` writes `spec/{ticket}/spec.md`, `plan.md`, and `development-summary.md`, sets `planned`, implements → `developed`, pushes `deploy_staging`, then `staging`. Detail page lists those files via `GET /feedback/ticket/:ticket/spec-docs` (JWT; reads monorepo `spec/` or `FEEDBACK_SPEC_ROOT`). Super admin sets all statuses via JWT `platform_role`. After a real status change, Support fire-and-forgets ticket details to `FEEDBACK_FIX_TRIGGER_URL` (localhost CLI listener); `ready_to_develop` → `/feedback-fix {ticket}`. MCP: `tooling/support-feedback-mcp` (hosted API only; `GET /feedback/ticket/:ticketNumber`). Reporters and super admin may **edit** reports (`PATCH /feedback/:id`); signed-in users **comment** (`POST /feedback/:id/comments`); unread comment counts on list. Comment notification emails via **Email** internal API (`EMAIL_API_BASE_URL`, `EMAIL_SERVICE_API_KEY`); platform template slug `feedback_comment` (edit in Email → Templates). Reporter comments notify `SUPER_ADMIN_EMAIL` (same `production.env` value as Identity / WebOnOne).
- Articles in `frontend/src/content/en/**/*.md` and `frontend/src/content/si/**/*.md` (Sinhala mirrors English paths; missing `si` file falls back to English).
- Help article bodies are not stored in MySQL (Markdown at build time).

